{# THE SHEETS EVERY AREA SCREEN NEEDS.

   Ordered shell → area, weakest to strongest: this bundle's sheet is the one
   allowed to override the platform's frame, so it is last. The shell's own
   sheet is linked by the shell's document; this adds only the area vocabulary
   on top of it — the plate tab, the identity band, the register's rows, the
   attention list and the honest-absent slot.

   Named through the bundle's constant rather than typed out, because anyone
   theming these screens has to be able to name the file and a path spelled
   twice is a path that goes stale once. #}
{# AND THE WIDGET SHEET, because an area's overview is a COMPOSED surface:
   its grid, its cells and their spans are the shell's widget vocabulary, the
   same one the team's screens and the library draw. A page that laid its
   cells out with `.w-grid` and did not link the sheet that defines it would
   be twelve cards in one column.

   Ordered widget → area, weakest to strongest: this bundle's sheet is the
   one allowed to override, and it is last. #}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset(constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\ShellBundle\\ShellBundle::WIDGET_STYLESHEET')) }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset(constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\AreaBundle\\AreaBundle::STYLESHEET')) }}">
